mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></msub><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>890</mn><mo>.3</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>kJ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><br />Based on the above thermochemical equations, the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></msub><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>298</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> for the reaction<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>graphite</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced></math> will be:"
